{"SelectedCalendarRepository.updateManyByCredentialId is called with an empty update object, which may be rejected by Prisma at runtime since update operations generally require at least one field to update. If the intent is to bump updatedAt, explicitly set updatedAt in the update data.": 0.9257581830024719, "The handler throws a generic Error instead of a typed tRPC error (e.g., TRPCError with an appropriate code like NOT_FOUND/FORBIDDEN), making it harder for clients to distinguish 'not found/access denied' from other failures.": 0.7402363419532776, "cacheUpdatedAt is typed as Date | null, but values coming from tRPC are commonly serialized as strings unless explicitly transformed, requiring defensive handling of non-Date inputs.": 0.365977019071579, "Intl.DateTimeFormat is hardcoded to 'en-US' rather than using the active locale, which can lead to inconsistent UX across different locales.": 0.7249299883842468}